From 6a78ce93ba4dfe25d94b6f5d78f5f7b41bc2e3d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenWorlds <openworlds@localhost>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 14:44:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/18] System properties, daemon threads and the command line,
 as a JVM

System keeps its properties in a Properties table (getProperties,
setProperties, setProperty, clearProperty) filled from the platform
(java.version 1.8.0, os.name, user.dir, file.encoding...); out and err can
be replaced (setOut, setErr); getenv reads the environment. Threads take
the daemon flag of their creator and setDaemon works; once main returns
the program goes on while a thread that is not a daemon runs; main gets
the command line. Thread.holdsLock, dumpStack, getThreadGroup;
Runtime.availableProcessors counts the cores, exec throws an IOException;
Integer.decode, Boolean.getBoolean, Float(String); AssertionError and
EOFException keep their messages.
